[list]
[*]Fixed: a colonist required at a ritual that began the moment they were called could spend it walking between the ceremony and their wardrobe. Stands change a colonist out of uniform when a job takes them out of the room, and a ritual looked like an ordinary job. It is not one: the ceremony can call them back mid-change, and the stand would send them off again. It also needed the leader to arrive before the colonist had finished changing, so a wardrobe across the base did it and one next door did not. Colonists held by a ritual, ceremony, party or caravan are now left alone. They attend in what they have on and change back afterwards, including the ones who used to make it in time.
[/list]
